# <type>: <what changed>  (imperative, lowercase, no period)
#
# Prefixes that matter (release on every merge to main):
#   feat:     new user-visible capability        -> minor bump
#   fix:      correcting wrong behavior          -> patch bump
#   chore:    tooling, CI, deps, no behavior     -> patch bump
#   docs:     documentation only                 -> patch bump
#   refactor: code change, no behavior change    -> patch bump
#
#   BREAKING CHANGE: <explanation> in the body   -> major bump
#
# Rule of thumb: "new or fixed?"  feat = new, fix = fixed, else chore.
#
# Example:
#   feat: add per-user exclusion list
